# Cloudflare Pages header rules.

# Cloudflare does not recognise the .webmanifest extension and serves it with
# no Content-Type, which makes strict parsers (PWABuilder, some browsers)
# reject the manifest.
/manifest.webmanifest
  Content-Type: application/manifest+json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

# The service worker must never be cached, or a redeploy can leave users stuck
# on an old shell indefinitely.
/sw.js
  Content-Type: text/javascript; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate
  Service-Worker-Allowed: /

# Digital Asset Links, used by the Android APK to prove it owns this domain.
# Served from the root and rewritten by _redirects, because Cloudflare Pages
# drops dot-directories on deploy.
/assetlinks.json
  Content-Type: application/json
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *

/.well-known/assetlinks.json
  Content-Type: application/json
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *

/icons/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

# Baseline hardening. This app holds private research and an auth session.
# CSP: scripts/styles only from self + the CDNs the app actually uses
# (esm.sh for the Supabase client, Google Fonts for Inter); Supabase itself
# is the only allowed fetch/XHR target besides same-origin. Data is rendered
# from Supabase content into the DOM, so this is a real second line of
# defense against injected-content XSS, not just a checkbox.
#
# Phase 55 added api.mapbox.com (script/style/connect) and worker-src blob:
# for the Map page's optional Satellite toggle (satellite-map.js). This is a
# deliberate, explicit exception to the img-src 'self' data: rule the Map
# page's own SVG basemap comment (see explore.js) has documented since Phase
# 53/54: a real satellite/terrain basemap means SOME third party (Mapbox)
# necessarily learns the map tiles a signed-in user's browser requests, which
# is the exact leak that rule existed to prevent. Marc explicitly chose this
# trade-off (real satellite/terrain, as a toggle alongside the existing
# same-origin map, not a replacement for it) after it was raised to him
# directly - see CLAUDE.md's Phase 55 section. The same-origin map remains
# the default and needs no third party at all; Satellite is opt-in per
# session, per click. events.mapbox.com (Mapbox's own telemetry ping) is
# deliberately NOT allowlisted - blocking it doesn't break map tiles, and
# there's no reason to let a second Mapbox endpoint see anything.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://esm.sh https://api.mapbox.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com https://api.mapbox.com; font-src https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://api.mapbox.com; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co https://esm.sh https://api.mapbox.com https://*.tiles.mapbox.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
